lesson: 84
title: Sharing equally
stars: 0
explain: To share things equally means every one gets the same number.
explain: Divide the total by the number of people (or groups) to find how many each one gets.
explain: 24 cookies shared among 4 children give each child 24 ÷ 4 = 6 cookies.
vars: a=name t=thing g=2..9 e=2..10
let: n = g * e
answer: n / g
exercise: {a} shares {n} {t} equally among {g} friends. How many {t} does each friend get?
exercise: There are {n} {t} and {g} children. Each child gets the same number. How many {t} does each child get?
exercise: {a} puts {n} {t} into {g} bags, the same number in each bag. How many {t} are in each bag?
exercise: {n} {t} are divided equally into {g} boxes. How many {t} go in each box?
exercise: {g} friends share {n} {t} fairly. How many {t} does each friend get?
test: How many {t} will be in each of {g} equal piles made from {n} {t}?
test: {a} has {n} {t} and wants to give every one of {g} classmates an equal share. How many {t} is one share?
test: The teacher splits {n} {t} evenly between {g} tables. How many {t} land on each table?
test: Each of {g} baskets gets an equal number of the {n} {t} {a} collected. How many {t} are in one basket?
exercise: {a} divides {n} {t} equally among {g} friends. How many {t} does each one get?
exercise: How many {t} does each child get when {n} {t} are shared equally by {g} children?
exercise: {g} cousins in Ohio share {n} {t} so that everyone gets the same. How many {t} does each cousin get?
exercise: {n} {t} are split evenly into {g} bags. How many {t} are in every bag?
exercise: {a} hands out {n} {t} to {g} classmates, the same number apiece. How many {t} does each classmate get?
exercise: A teacher in London puts {n} {t} into {g} equal groups. How many {t} are in each group?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t} and puts the same number on each of {g} plates. How many {t} go on one plate?
exercise: {g} friends in Sydney get {n} {t} in all and share them fairly. How many {t} does each friend get?
test: If {n} {t} are given out fairly to {g} children, what is each child's share?
test: {a} empties a bag of {n} {t} into {g} bowls, filling each bowl equally. How many {t} end up in a bowl?
test: A coach in Toronto splits {n} players into {g} equal teams. How many players are on each team?
test: {n} {t} make {g} equal rows. How many {t} are in a row?
test: In Wellington, {g} brothers and sisters share {n} dollars equally. How many dollars does each of them get?
test: Each of {g} boxes ends up with the same number of {t}, and there are {n} {t} in total. How many {t} does one box get?
